# Obstacle avoidance fed by the Pi. Loaded on top of vedc_buoy.parm only when the Pi code runs
# (run_boat.sh --pi): with PRX1_TYPE set and nobody sending OBSTACLE_DISTANCE, ArduPilot's
# pre-arm check refuses to arm, which is right on the boat and a nuisance for a simulator
# session with Mission Planner alone.
#
# The Pi sends LiDAR clusters and keep-out circles around people already attended
# (Rasp_Pi/modules/obstacle_feed.py); BendyRuler bends the path around them in AUTO and GUIDED.
PRX1_TYPE       2       # MAVLink
OA_TYPE         1       # BendyRuler
OA_BR_LOOKAHEAD 5       # the default 15 m is beyond the LiDAR's 8 m
OA_MARGIN_MAX   1.0     # clearance BendyRuler keeps; 1.5 would not let the boat between the tree and the houses
# Simple avoidance (stop short of what the LiDAR sees) off, fence only. While it limits the speed
# near an obstacle Rover refuses to turn at low speed (mode.cpp, navigate_to_waypoint), so the boat
# could not pivot away from the obstacle BendyRuler was steering it around, and stayed there.
AVOID_ENABLE    1
# BendyRuler often asks for a heading far off the bow (around an obstacle the boat has already
# closed on). Without pivot turns Rover answers a large heading error with zero speed, and a
# boat at zero speed does not turn: it sat still for minutes. Above 60 deg it now turns on the
# spot with the rear motors, one ahead and one astern. Needs reversible rear ESCs on the boat.
WP_PIVOT_ANGLE  60
WP_PIVOT_RATE   40
